    {
      "id": "yxqraoq",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "12.3 Important Mnemonics"
    },
    {
      "id": "ph91t3m",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "KHARIF crops (June–Oct): RAM-CGS-JBS = Rice, Arhar, Maize, Cotton, Groundnut, Soybean, Jowar, Bajra, Sunflower",
        "RABI crops (Oct–Mar): WBG-ML = Wheat, Barley, Gram, Mustard, Linseed (Flax)",
        "Plant Nutrients Macro: N-P-K-Ca-Mg-S (Never Pause; Keep Calcium Magnesium Strong)",
        "Plant Nutrients Micro: Fe-Mn-Zn-Cu-B-Mo-Cl-Ni (Farmers Manage Zinc Copper By Molybdenum Chloride Nicely)",
        "Soil Horizons (top to bottom): O-A-B-C-R (Old Aged Bedrocked Creatures Rest)",
        "Types of erosion by water: Splash → Sheet → Rill → Gully (SSRG) — severity increases",
        "Seed classes (Foundation→Certified): Breeder (Golden) → Foundation (White) → Certified (Blue)",
        "NABARD stands for: National Bank for Agriculture and Rural Development (est. 12 July 1982)",
        "FAO's 4 food security pillars: AAUSA — Availability, Access, Utilisation, Stability, Agency (new 5th pillar 2021)",
        "BSY cost: A1 A2 B1 B2 C1 C2 C3 — C2+50% is MSP formula (CACP)"
      ]
    },
